== Source-family audit ==

* '''Wikipedia''' — public terminology, redirects, history and discovery; not primary support for formal claims.
* '''Scholarpedia''' — direct broad coverage is sparse; use only specialized articles that genuinely match a descendant concept.
* '''Primary/scholarly''' — Gruber; Studer/Benjamins/Fensel; Davis/Shrobe/Szolovits; Brachman/Levesque; Quillian; Description Logic Handbook; Hogan et al.
* '''Standards''' — W3C RDF/RDFS/OWL/SKOS; ISO/IEC 21838; ISO 25964; NISO/DCMI metadata guidance.

== Phase-1 decisions ==

# [[Property]] is broad concept first, RDF/OWL application second.
# [[Category]] is not silently normalized to formal [[Class]].
# [[Concept]] and [[Entity]] remain distinct.
# [[Knowledge graph]] does not universally require a formal ontology.
# [[Semantic network]] remains a standalone historical/KR concept.
# [[Schema]] is not modeled after RDFS alone.
# RDF 1.2 is described as Candidate Recommendation in 2026, not as a finalized Recommendation.

